       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, almost four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day. A single 5000 mg dose is also above the usual maximum single dose of 1000 mg. At that level the risk of serious hepatotoxicity is high, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** PO three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** PO three times daily (1.95 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n\nMany services cap at 3 g/day, and a 70 kg patient with normal liver function could go up to 4 g/day. Tell me the dose and frequency you want, and any note to add, such as PRN or a maximum daily dose. I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 5000 mg, please confirm, though I'd advise against it."
      }
