       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 15 g/day is a toxic dose, and a single 5000 mg dose is also well above the safe range. It could cause acute liver failure, and nothing you've described about the patient (70 kg, normal liver and kidney function, no allergies) makes it safe.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours, or 500 mg PO three times daily\n\nIf you're after a particular effect, such as stronger analgesia or fever control, I can enter an adjunct instead. If the 5000 mg came from a protocol or another order, please check it with your attending or the pharmacist. If the patient may have taken an overdose, that needs a separate workup, including a serum acetaminophen level and poison control or NAC consideration, and not a scheduled order like this one.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
